grad requires a scalar floating output

A KNOWN REGRESSION, pinned deliberately. Against the f32-only module this file
evaluated to 0.8787825. Making the module generic means `erf` names an
uninstantiated generic, and `grad` cannot fix its dtype from a point-free
argument, so the same source is now rejected at checking.

The workaround is eta-expansion, which works at both dtypes and is covered by
`test_f32_grad_through_a_wrapper_still_works` and
`test_f64_grad_through_a_wrapper_works`:

    def erf_at(x: f32) -> f32 = erf(x)
    (grad(erf_at))(0.5f32)

If a compiler release makes the point-free form work again, this case reports
an unexpected pass. Delete it then, and drop the caveat from
docs/book/src/special/overview.md in the same change.
